act information should be used. Emergency: 911 Riverside County Search & Rescue: (951) 955-4930 Agua Caliente Tribal Ranger: 760.831.0045', NULL, NULL, TRUE, FALSE);
INSERT INTO trails (trail_id, trail_name, alternate_names, desert_riders_trail, bookable, area, park, trailhead_name, trailhead_gps, parking_notes, distance_mi, elevation_gain_ft, highest_point_ft, est_time_easy_pace, est_time_strong_pace, difficulty, activity_type, route_type, technical_rating, optimal_season, viable_season, avoid_season, heat_considerations, water_sources_on_trail, kid_friendly, min_age_rec, dog_friendly, good_for_beginners, good_for_athletes, opening_description, what_makes_it_special, best_for_attributes, trail_day_tip, ridewithgps_link, strava_link, garmin_connect_link, gpx_file_location, photo_references, known_hazards, cell_coverage, emergency_egress_notes, nearest_neighborhood, drive_time_from_downtown_ps, entry_fee_required, guided_eligible) VALUES ('TRAIL-037', 'Fern Canyon Loop', NULL, FALSE, TRUE, 'Indian Canyons / South Palm Springs', 'Indian Canyons', 'Victor Trail', NULL, 'Inside of Indian Canyons.  Park entry fee required.  Per person rates.  Paved parking lot at the Indian Canyons Ranger Station.', 5.4, 831, 1498, '3 - 4 hrs', '1 - 1.5 hrs', 4, 'Hiking, Trail Running', 'Loop', 3, ARRAY['Jan','Feb','Mar','Nov','Dec','Apr','Oct']::TEXT[], ARRAY['May','Sep']::TEXT[], ARRAY['Jun','Jul','Aug']::TEXT[], 'Exposed with little shade. Start by 8:30am in shoulder season.  Indian Canyons doesn''t open until 8am.', 'None. Bring minimum 2L of water per person.', FALSE, '16+', 'No', FALSE, TRUE, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Big Views','Solitude and quiet','Photography opportunities','Interesting geology']::TEXT[], NULL, 'https://ridewithgps.com/routes/56730491?privacy_code=QHT6vNZ7yXqTopjc00IKq5hokxdZWzVA', NULL, 'https://connect.garmin.com/app/activity/21796404628', NULL, NULL, 'Steep climbs and descents alongside exposed cliffs.  Exposed terrain and lack of shade increase the risk of heat exposure.  Backcountry travel with few other people present.', '3 - Fair', 'In emergencies, the below contact information should be used. Emergency: 911 Riverside County Search & Rescue: (951) 955-4930 Agua Caliente Tribal Ranger: 760.831.0045', NULL, NULL, TRUE, FALSE);
INSERT INTO trails (trail_id, trail_name, alternate_names, desert_riders_trail, bookable, area, park, trailhead_name, trailhead_gps, parking_notes, distance_mi, elevation_gain_ft, highest_point_ft, est_time_easy_pace, est_time_strong_pace, difficulty, activity_type, route_type, technical_rating, optimal_season, viable_season, avoid_season, heat_considerations, water_sources_on_trail, kid_friendly, min_age_rec, dog_friendly, good_for_beginners, good_for_athletes, opening_description, what_makes_it_special, best_for_attributes, trail_day_tip, ridewithgps_link, strava_link, garmin_connect_link, gpx_file_location, photo_references, known_hazards, cell_coverage, emergency_egress_notes, nearest_neighborhood, drive_time_from_downtown_ps, entry_fee_required, guided_eligible) VALUES ('TRAIL-038', 'East Fork Out & Back', NULL, FALSE, TRUE, 'Indian Canyons / South Palm Springs', 'Indian Canyons', 'Palm Canyon', NULL, 'Inside of Indian Canyons.  Park entry fee required.  Per person rates.  Paved parking lot at the Indian Canyons Ranger Station.', 5.6, 789, 1554, '3 - 4 hrs', '1.5 - 2 hrs', 3, 'Hiking, Trail Running', 'Out & Back', 4, ARRAY['Jan','Feb','Mar','Nov','Dec','Oct']::TEXT[], ARRAY['May','Sep','Apr']::TEXT[], ARRAY['Jun','Jul','Aug']::TEXT[], 'Exposed with little shade. Start by 8:30am in shoulder season.  Indian Canyons doesn''t open until 8am.', 'None. Bring minimum 2L of water per person.', FALSE, '16+', 'No', FALSE, TRUE, NULL, NULL, ARRAY['Solitude and quiet','Big Views','Interesting geology','Wildlife and nature','Photography opportunities']::TEXT[], NULL, 'https://ridewithgps.com/routes/56730519?privacy_code=afhyQEokgKZ22mn7LnHYXhQe3ofBwPIL', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sandy washes, boulder scrambles, and sun exposure are prevalent on this route.', '3 - Fair', 'In emergencies, the below contact information should be used. Emergency: 911 Riverside County Search & Rescue: (951) 955-4930 Agua Caliente Tribal Ranger: 760.831.0045', NULL, NULL, TRUE, FALSE);
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 1, 'Canyon Wash Entry', 0.5, 'The trail descends into a sandy wash marked by high canyon walls and desert lavender. The smell of the wash after rain, birdsong before the heat arrives. The world slows down here before the trail asks anything of you.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 2, 'Bob Hope House Lookout', 2.4, 'A left turn onto Berns Trail opens a unique, rarely-seen view of Bob Hope''s hilltop residence across the canyon. The angle exists at this moment on the trail and nowhere else.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 3, 'The Quiet Valley', 2.7, 'The Berns descent drops into a quiet valley almost no one reaches. Rarely visited, unhurried, with a view through the valley floor toward Palm Springs. Pause before the climb back out.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 4, 'Cahuilla Peak Junction', 3.2, 'The unmarked left turn continues the loop. Straight ahead is Cahuilla Peak; an optional extension with wider views of Palm Springs. Worth the detour if energy allows; return to this point to continue.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 5, 'The San Jacinto View', 4, 'Back on the Bogert return, San Jacinto fills the horizon. The descent to the trailhead begins here.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 1, 'Desert Riders Trail Signs', 0.1, 'A pair of Desert Riders trail signs mark the split at the trailhead: Earl Henderson to the left, Garstin to the right. Take the left. You''ll finish from the right.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 2, 'Bob Hope House Switchback', 1.5, 'A switchback on the Shannon Trail delivers an unexpected view of Bob Hope''s hilltop residence across the canyon, from an angle that exists nowhere else in Palm Springs. Take a breather here.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 3, 'Shannon-Berns Intersection', 2.1, 'The top of the climb. Shannon Trail meets Berns Trail at a T intersection. Optional left turn to Cahuilla Peak for wider views of Palm Springs. Return to this point to continue the loop. The major climbing is done.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 4, 'Garstin Descent', 2.3, 'The trail transitions onto Garstin for the return to the trailhead. The terrain opens and the descent begins.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 1, 'Rock Heart', 1, 'A heart shaped from dark volcanic rocks faces out over the city from the ridgeline. You''ll pass it again on the return.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 2, 'Jane''s Hoffbrau', 1.2, 'The canyon bottom. Fan palms, a broad granite chute carved by water runoff, ferns in the cracks. Named by the Desert Riders and still feels like a secret. The most transporting moment on the loop. Take a pause before the climb back out.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 3, 'Desert Riders Trail Sign', 1.5, 'The junction: Jane''s Hoffbrau behind you, Clara Burgess to the right. Do not follow the sign. Go up the hill to the right to return to the dirt road and complete the loop.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 4, 'Rock Heart (return)', 1.8, 'The dirt road brings you past the rock heart again from the other direction. From here the trail follows the dirt road and then transitions back to single track for the descent to the trailhead.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 1, 'Rocks on Palm Tree Stump', 0.1, 'A small stack of rocks on a palm tree stump marks the entry to the hidden trail. Easy to miss from the road. Cross the wash and climb the switchbacks on the far side. This is where the real trail begins.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 2, 'The Hidden Canyon', 0.3, 'Above the wash, the hidden canyon comes into view for the first time. The trail runs its edge rather than descending into it. It was invisible from the road and from the wash. It reveals itself only to people who climbed far enough to find it.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 3, 'Rock Cairn', 1, 'A carefully stacked cairn alongside the trail. Chest high, built with real intention over many visits by someone you''ll never know. Optional short detour to reach it. Worth a long pause.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 4, 'Desert Riders Oasis', 3.9, 'The turnaround. Picnic tables on a wide sandy flat, agave reaching skyward, San Jacinto and the Santa Rosa range filling the horizon. And in the middle of it: a bulldozer, left exactly where it stopped working when Dunn Road was built. Nobody brought it down. It never left.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 1, 'North Lykken Trail Picnic Tables', 0.2, 'Picnic tables at the top of the opening rock scramble mark the transition from the neighborhood into the trail system proper. The city is already below you. The real climb starts here.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 2, 'The Alluvial Fan', 0.8, 'The trail enters a wide alluvial fan — loose stone, desert scrub, lizards moving through the rocks. The debris field of the mountain above, spread out and sorted by water over thousands of years. The plant diversity here is unlike anywhere else on the route.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 3, 'O''Donnell Golf Course Overlook', 2.2, 'The trail turns sharply right and the city opens below. O''Donnell Golf Course in the foreground, downtown Palm Springs behind it, the historic Las Palmas and Vista Las Palmas neighborhoods to the left. This is the above-the-city moment the climb has been building toward.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 4, 'Skyline Trail Picnic Tables', 2.9, 'Picnic tables on the Skyline Trail with wide views in both directions. The turnaround point. Good moment for a snack before the return.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 5, 'Mountain-top Pull-up Bar', 3, 'A pull-up bar on top of a mountain just off the Skyline Trail. No signage, no explanation. Someone put it there and it stayed. Worth the short detour to find it.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 1, 'Bighorn Sheep Rock', 0.6, 'A ledge below the trail where bighorn sheep gather most mornings, unbothered, with the full valley arranged behind them. Stop quietly and watch before they notice you.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 2, 'Tahquitz Falls Viewpoint', 1, 'The falls appear with no warning. You come around a corner and a white thread of water drops through dark rock into the shadowed canyon far below. The scale is made stranger by the severity of the dropoff at your feet. Most people stop here to admire the view without planning on it.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 3, 'South Lykken Picnic Tables', 1.5, 'Six weathered picnic tables on an open saddle looking southeast toward Palm Canyon and the Santa Rosa Mountains. The birds are loud up here. The city is not. The turnaround point, and worth a long pause before the descent.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-029', 1, 'Plant Life Corridor', 0.3, 'The alluvial fan supports one of the densest concentrations of desert plant life on any trail in this library: encelia, desert lavender, cheesebush, beavertail, cholla, barrel cactus. Low enough to examine at any height, close enough to touch. Slow down here.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-029', 2, 'Summit Boulder', 0.6, 'Several large boulders sit next to the trail near the far end of the loop with views back out of the canyon toward Palm Springs and the wind turbines in the distance. A good place to stop, eat something, and let the quiet settle before the return.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 1, 'Andreas Creek Wading Spot', 0.1, 'The creek broadens here and cascades down several large boulders into a shallow pool with pebbles underneath. Knee-deep in most conditions. Take your shoes off. This is the point of the trail.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 2, 'Andreas Club Buildings', 0.4, 'Historic structures visible from the upper trail, remnants of the early desert club era tucked into the canyon above the creek. Easy to walk past without noticing. Worth a pause to place yourself in time.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 3, 'Bridge over Andreas Creek', 0.5, 'The wooden bridge crosses Andreas Creek and transitions the loop from the shaded canyon side to the sunny upper trail. An elevated view of the canyon walls and palm trees awaits after this crossing.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 1, 'Palm Grove Entry', 0.5, 'The trail leaves the fire road and enters the canyon proper. The palms close in, the air cools, and the creek becomes audible before it''s visible. The transition from open desert to canyon shade is immediate.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 2, 'Side Quest: Seven Falls', 1.2, 'The canyon continues up to Seven Falls, adding approximately 1.2 miles to the total. In winter and spring: stream crossings, running waterfalls, a genuinely different experience. In summer and fall: a desert wash hike with boulder scrambles. Worth it if energy allows. Budget accordingly before committing.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 3, 'Canyon Exit', 1.2, 'The loop turns left onto Coffman Trail and begins the ridge climb. The creek and palms are below and behind you from here.');
INSERT INTO trail_landmarks (trail_id, seq, name, mile, description) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 4, 'Ridge Viewpoint', 1.5, 'The ridge opens to a wide view of the Coachella Valley: Palm Springs small in the distance, the Santa Rosa Mountains layered across the horizon, the palm grove threading through the canyon floor below. This is what the climb was for.');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 1, 0, 'Bogert Trail trailhead. Dirt parking lot. Trail begins heading south.', '33.7890° N, 116.5214° W', NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 2, 0.3, 'Enter canyon wash. Sandy footing. Desert lavender fragrance in cool months. Wide and easy to cross — continue straight through.', NULL, 'Sensory landmark — slow down here');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 3, 0.8, 'Trail steepens. Switchbacks begin climbing toward ridgeline. San Jacinto starts to appear above.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 4, 1.3, 'Wildhorse Trail junction. Signed. Continue STRAIGHT — do not turn. Last signed marker on the loop.', NULL, 'Navigation note — easy to miss');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 5, 1.6, 'Unmarked T intersection. Take RIGHT. Follow toward the high point ahead.', NULL, 'No signage — guide required');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 6, 2.1, 'Bob Hope Viewpoint. Full panorama opens. His former residence visible below. Palm Springs Airport beyond. San Jacinto east. Pause here.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 7, 2.4, 'Optional: Trail continues to Cahuilla Hills Peak (1,522 ft). Cairn at summit. Return to viewpoint before continuing. Do not go past cairn.', NULL, 'Side quest — optional');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 8, 2.6, 'Berns Trail begins. Descend from ridgeline into valley. Trail unmarked. Follow the descent southwest.', NULL, 'Route transition point');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 9, 3.1, 'Valley floor. Cross the wash. Rocky footing — take your time. Switchback climb begins immediately on far side.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 10, 3.6, 'Top of switchbacks. Unmarked junction — take LEFT fork onto small trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note — critical turn');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 11, 4.2, 'Rejoin Wildhorse / Bogert junction. Take RIGHT onto Bogert Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-001', 12, 5.18, 'Bogert Trail trailhead. Return to parking lot. San Jacinto lit behind you on the descent.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 2, 0.1, 'Sharp left onto Earl Henderson Trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 3, 0.1, 'Landmark A — Desert Riders Trail Signs. Take the Earl Henderson Trail to the left; you''ll finish the loop on the Garstin Trail from the right.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 4, 1, 'Keep straight onto Earl Henderson Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 5, 1.1, 'Sharp right onto Shannon Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 6, 1.5, 'Landmark B — Bob Hope House Switchback. A truly unique view of Bob Hope''s hilltop home — take a breather and enjoy it.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 7, 2.1, 'Landmark C — Shannon-Berns Intersection. The Shannon Trail meets the Berns Trail here. Optional left turn to the top of Cahuilla Peak for a quick side quest with more Palm Springs views.', NULL, 'Side quest — optional');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 8, 2.1, 'At the T intersection, turn slight right onto Berns Trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 9, 2.3, 'Continue straight onto Garstin Trail, then continue right on Garstin Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 10, 3.4, 'Keep left onto Garstin Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-002', 11, 3.5, 'End of route. Back at the trailhead.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 2, 0.3, 'Right onto Palm Hills Trail, taking the single track up the hill.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 3, 0.7, 'Keep left, then continue onto the dirt road up the hill.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 4, 0.8, 'Follow the dirt road left and down the small hill, then continue straight on the dirt road.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 5, 1, 'Landmark A — Rock Heart. A heart shape formed out of rocks — a landmark you''ll revisit on the return.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 6, 1.1, 'Left onto the single track trail, which descends toward the canyon and a desert wash at the bottom.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 7, 1.2, 'Landmark B — Jane''s Hoffbrau. A quiet pause spot with a collection of palm trees, a granite "rock slide" carved by years of water runoff, and an intimate place to breathe.', NULL, 'Sensory landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 8, 1.5, 'Right-hand turn up the hill when you see the Desert Riders trail sign marking Jane''s Hoffbrau and the Clara Burgess Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 9, 1.5, 'Landmark C — Desert Riders Trail Sign. Marks Jane''s Hoffbrau (where you came from) to the left and the Clara Burgess Trail to the right. Don''t follow the sign — instead go up the hill to the right to head back to the dirt road.', NULL, 'Navigation note — counterintuitive turn, easy to follow the wrong sign');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 10, 1.8, 'Slight right onto Eagle Canyon Trail, then continue straight onto the dirt road.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 11, 2.3, 'Follow the dirt road past the rock heart, around the corner, then keep left onto the Palm Hills single track.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 12, 2.5, 'Continue straight on the Palm Hills Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 13, 2.7, 'Left onto the dirt road, heading back to the parking lot (the single track eventually reconnects to the same point but is more scenic).', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-008', 14, 3, 'End of route. Back at the trailhead.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 2, 0.1, 'Landmark A — Rocks on Palm Tree Stump. A stack of rocks marks the otherwise-hidden trail entrance. Turn left and drop down into the wash.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 3, 0.3, 'Cross the wash and climb the rocky switchbacks on the far side (Landmark B — The Hidden Canyon). Sharp right turn at the top onto the main trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note — trail is easy to miss without the rock-stack marker');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 4, 1, 'Steep climb alongside the trail. Watch and listen for mountain bikers on this stretch.', NULL, 'Caution — shared trail with mountain bikers');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 5, 1, 'Landmark C — Rock Cairn. A stacked rock marker and significant waypoint; optional short detour to view it up close.', NULL, 'Side quest — optional / Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 6, 3.9, 'Right onto Art Smith Trail, continuing into Desert Riders Oasis.', NULL, 'Navigation note — major junction');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 7, 3.9, 'Landmark D — Desert Riders Oasis. A place of Desert Riders legacy, built on a sand flat with views to San Jacinto and the Santa Rosa mountains. An old bulldozer left from the construction of Dunn Road sits at the edge.', NULL, 'Primary landmark — destination point');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 8, 6.8, 'Slight right, beginning the return leg.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 9, 7.7, 'Right, cross back over the wash, and climb up the hidden trail toward the vehicle.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-015', 10, 7.9, 'End of route. Back at the trailhead.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 2, 0.2, 'Landmark A — Picnic Tables. Picnic tables at the top of a small scramble.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 3, 0.8, 'Landmark B — The Alluvial Fan. Entrance to the alluvial fan, with a wide variety of plants, lizards, birds, and stones.', NULL, 'Sensory landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 4, 1.6, 'Slight right, then left to stay on the trail, then right (look for the small trail sign to confirm), then slight right continuing onto North Lykken Trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note — several turns, watch for trail sign');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 5, 2.2, 'Sharp right onto North Lykken Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 6, 2.2, 'Landmark C — O''Donnell Golf Course Overlook. Views across the golf course and downtown Palm Springs; the historic Las Palmas and Little Tuscany neighborhoods visible to the left.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 7, 2.8, 'Right, then continue straight to stay on North Lykken Trail, then left onto Skyline Trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 8, 2.8, 'Slight right onto Skyline Trail toward the hidden pull-up bar.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 9, 2.9, 'Landmark D — Picnic Tables. A second set of picnic tables along the Skyline Trail — a good spot to enjoy the view or grab a snack.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 10, 2.9, 'Landmark E — Mountain-top Pull-up Bar. Right turn to visit the hidden pull-up bar just off the trail.', NULL, 'Side quest / fun stop');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 11, 3, 'Make a U-turn at the pull-up bar and return to the picnic tables on Skyline Trail to begin the return trip.', NULL, 'Route transition point — begin return');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 12, 3.1, 'After passing the picnic tables, turn right toward North Lykken Trail, then sharp right onto North Lykken Trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 13, 3.6, 'Sharp left to stay on North Lykken Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 14, 4.3, 'Climb up the boulder and turn left immediately to stay on North Lykken Trail, then right to stay on North Lykken Trail.', NULL, 'Navigation note — boulder scramble, easy to miss turn');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-016', 15, 5.8, 'End of route. Back at the trailhead.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-029', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-029', 2, 0.4, 'Keep left.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-029', 3, 0.6, 'Keep left.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-029', 4, 0.7, 'Sharp left.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-029', 5, 1.2, 'End of route. Back at the trailhead.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 2, 0.5, 'Keep right, then right again onto Coffman Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 3, 0.5, 'Sharp left onto Murray Canyon Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 4, 1.2, 'Landmark A — Side Quest: Seven Falls. Continue up Murray Canyon to visit Seven Falls; adds about 1.2 miles round trip to the total hike.', NULL, 'Side quest — optional');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 5, 2.3, 'Right onto Coffman Trail.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-033', 6, 2.6, 'End of route. Back at the trailhead.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 2, 0.1, 'Landmark 1 — Andreas Creek Wading Spot. The creek broadens here and cascades down several large boulders into a shallow pool with pebbles underneath. Knee-deep in most conditions. Take your shoes off.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 3, 0.4, 'Landmark 2 — Andreas Club Buildings. Historic structures visible from the upper trail, remnants of the early desert club era tucked into the canyon above the creek.', NULL, 'Historical landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 4, 0.5, 'Landmark 3 — Bridge over Andreas Creek. The wooden bridge crosses Andreas Creek, transitioning the loop from the shaded canyon side to the sunny upper trail.', NULL, 'Route transition point');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-032', 5, 0.9, 'End of route. Back at the trailhead.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 1, 0, 'Trailhead. Start of route. (Street parking on Mesquite is a separate 0.75 mi approach walk not reflected in the mile markers below.)', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 2, 0.6, 'Landmark 1 — Bighorn Sheep Rock. A ledge below the trail where bighorn sheep gather most mornings, unbothered, with the full valley arranged behind them.', NULL, 'Wildlife landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 3, 1, 'Landmark 2 — Tahquitz Falls Viewpoint. The falls appear with no warning — a white thread of water dropping through dark rock into the shadowed canyon far below.', NULL, 'Primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 4, 1.5, 'Landmark 3 — South Lykken Picnic Tables. Six weathered picnic tables on an open saddle looking southeast toward Palm Canyon and the Santa Rosa Mountains. Turnaround point.', NULL, 'Turnaround point — primary landmark');
INSERT INTO trail_waypoints (trail_id, waypoint_num, mile_marker, description, gps_coordinates, notes) VALUES ('TRAIL-022', 5, 2.7, 'End of route. Retrace the trail back to the trailhead (out and back).', NULL, NULL);
