-- ---------- pricing_tiers ----------
-- Experience-tier rows (trail/p2p/custom): tier_id and prices match the three
-- live TIERS objects this table consolidates (Section 4.13) -- api/create-
-- payment-intent.js, api/create-deposit-hold.js, and lib/finalize-kit-
-- change.js all agree exactly. tier_id matches the live tierKey strings
-- ('trail','p2p') so experience_bookings.tier's live values need no rename.
-- 'custom' has no fixed price (sold by contact/quote) -- seeded at 0/0 as a
-- placeholder so the FK exists.
--
-- Membership-tier rows: Trail $399 confirmed against the live page before
-- this PRD locked; Summit $899 and Founding Member $1,499 (one-time)
-- confirmed against the live page during this build chat's prerequisite
-- check. Founding Member has a hard 50-spot cap (confirmed by Airey
-- 2026-08-31) -- capacity_total is set there and left NULL (uncapped)
-- everywhere else; see schema.sql's comment on pricing_tiers.capacity_total
-- for why remaining capacity is computed live rather than cached here.
--
-- Legacy ($2,999, one-time) is a real planned tier -- per Airey (2026-08-31)
-- it activates only after Founding Member's 50 spots sell out, and isn't
-- live/sellable yet. Seeded now so the row exists, following this codebase's
-- existing convention of keeping a not-yet-sellable tier's data present and
-- gating its activation in application code rather than deleting the row
-- (the same pattern already used for Peaks to Pools/Custom). Price is NOT
-- confirmed against a live page (Legacy isn't shown there yet) -- taken from
-- PSAC-project-context.md; flag to Airey before this tier is ever exposed
-- for real sale.

-- ---------- gear_units (45 rows; status reset to 'available', current_booking_id
-- cleared on every row per Section 7 -- the live 'checked out' state reflects only
-- test-booking activity, not real gear placement) ----------
--
-- All of this data is test data (confirmed by Airey 2026-08-31); the real
-- gear inventory is entered fresh next week and these rows get deleted and
-- replaced entirely. schema.sql keeps gear_units.unit_id as a simple global
-- primary key rather than widening it for this collision, so the 4 live
-- backpack_plus rows that reused backpack_standard's GP-0001..GP-0004 labels
-- are disambiguated here as GQ-0001..GQ-0004 (backpack_plus only;
-- backpack_standard keeps its original GP-0001..GP-0004). qr_token --
-- confirmed genuinely unique per physical item across all 45 live rows --
-- is unchanged and is still the right join key to reach for if any
-- QR-code-scanning code path needs the true physical-item identity.

